proxy for race. Excluding the race field while keeping those proxies can improve a model's measured performance precisely because historic discrimination is present in the data. The model objective must therefore be tested against the social consequences of its predictions, not just predictive accuracy.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithmic Fairness and Justice","Fairness Through Unawareness","aiethics.epub","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Proxy Discrimination.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Proxy Discrimination.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"proxy discrimination proxy discrimination","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Proxy Discrimination.md","fileName":"Proxy Discrimination.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Proxy Discrimination","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]\n\n[[datascience_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algorithmic Fairness and Justice","Fairness Through Unawareness","aiethics.epub","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}